  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Universal Protection Service Limited Partnership recorded $295M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Universal Protection Service Limited Partnership won 24 awards so far, with an average award size of $12.3M. Universal Protection Service Limited Partnership obligations are up 152.6% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $35.7M in FY21 to $45.5M in FY22, $86.3M in FY23, $86.9M in FY24, and $117M in FY25 before reaching $295M in FY26. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $248M in FY2026 to date. The Smithsonian Institution obligated $31.3M, the Department of Commerce obligated $15M, and the Department of State obligated $851K. The page reports contract obligations and award counts, and shows that current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. This profile is useful for contractors tracking where federal spending on security-related services and protections concentrates in the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations trend over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations rose steadily from FY21 through FY25 and then increased sharply in FY26. Obligations were $35.7M in FY21, $45.5M in FY22, $86.3M in FY23, $86.9M in FY24, $117M in FY25, and $295M in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer, obligating $248M in FY2026 to date. Other buyers include the Smithsonian Institution with $31.3M, the Department of Commerce with $15M, and the Department of State with $851K."
      }
    ]
  },
